<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/doc-template/templates/page">
<$fill $name="body">

!! Why don't bare `[[_index]]` refs work?

The namespace resolver expands pseudo-segments on the ref ITSELF, before walk-up runs. A bare `_index` has no preceding prefix, so the resolver can't find an index page. Use the absolute form `[[knowledge/topics/foo/_index]]` instead — the pseudo expands to `index` against the `knowledge/topics/foo` prefix.

!! How do I add a new alias?

Create a tiddler tagged `$:/tags/NamespaceAlias` with fields `short` (the ref users type) and `expands-to` (the rewritten ref). Example: `short=TS`, `expands-to=knowledge/topics/typescript`. Then `[[TS]]` resolves to that path. (Pattern aliases use `$:/tags/NamespacePatternAlias` with `pattern` regex + `replacement`.)

!! How do I disable walk-up?

Set `$:/config/rimir/namespace/walk-up` to `no`. Sibling-walk-up refs will then become unresolved unless their target is exact, aliased, or mounted.

!! What's a "stub"?

A note whose body is shorter than the stub threshold (default 200 characters; configurable in Settings). The `knowledge.stubs()` filter function returns them. There is no live UI consumer in 0.1.20+ — the Write maintenance tab was removed when the app collapsed to a single mindmap surface — but the function is still useful from the LLM tools and external probes.

!! How do I promote a note from fleeting to evergreen?

The dedicated tier-pill cycler was removed in 0.1.20 along with the section-based note view. Promote by:

* opening the popup-edit modal (✎ button in the mindmap preview pane → ''⛶ Edit''), or
* editing the `kn.tier` field directly from the field bar, or
* using an action chain (`<$action-setfield $tiddler=<<note>> kn.tier="evergreen"/>`).

The tier filter chips above the mindmap still read `kn.tier`, so the field is meaningful for filtering even without a dedicated promotion UI.

!! Can knowledge notes link back to orga / priv content?

Yes — write `[[orga/projects/foo]]` from a knowledge note. But the app does NOT surface backlinks FROM knowledge TO orga in the orga app (one-way coupling by design). Backlinks within the knowledge namespace work both ways.

!! Why are some nodes collapsed when I open the app?

The producer marks every node deeper than the area root with `core:collapsed=true` in the BASE MDOM so the initial view stays scannable. Expanding a node writes an override into the widget's overlay tiddler — so your expansions persist across reloads. Reset everything by deleting `$:/state/rimir/mindmap/kn-main/overlay`.

</$fill>
</$transclude>
